  "details": "We need this with (ideally) integration of eye tracking for updated ear muff mode. \n\nhttps://proactivehearing.cs.washington.edu/ \n\nThis is essentially what Meta is claiming to do with their smart glasses in regards to isolating audio based on the person who you're speaking to. tons of examples are shown there in the source code is currently public.\n\nI could totally see this being in combination with a speech to text overlay natively embedded into VR chat in the future, primarily for accessibility.\n\nThis is a tall ask I'm sure, And I'm not sure what the intentions of the Creator Companion app are outside of Hosting repositories for unity Related assets but potentially that may also be a good platform or something like this to be embedded in it to offload server resources.",
